   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How the passé composé is formed",
     "texto": [
      "It is formed with **avoir** or **être** in the present + past participle: **j'ai parlé**, **elle est arrivée**. Most verbs use **avoir**; several verbs of movement and reflexive verbs use **être**. Learn each verb with its auxiliary."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Basic agreement",
     "texto": [
      "With **être**, the past participle agrees with the subject: **il est arrivé**, **elle est arrivée**, **ils sont arrivés**. With **avoir**, at this level, it usually doesn't change: **elle a mangé**.",
      "Example: **Nous sommes allés au cinéma** / **Elles sont allées au cinéma**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Two pasts, two perspectives",
     "texto": [
      "The **imparfait** presents background, a description, a state or a habit. The **passé composé** presents a completed event or a series of events. It doesn't have to be sudden: **Hier, j'ai travaillé trois heures** is also a completed event.",
      "Example: **Il faisait beau quand le train est arrivé** (the weather was nice when the train arrived)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Two pasts, two uses",
